That approach is outdated and will not be followed here. As an authoritarian regime, only men should engage in heavy labor jobs to maintain order, while women should stay at home and focus on household activities. All other measures taken by the authorities are for the greater good of the society.

This policy is enforced to ensure that women and children remain within their domestic roles, which includes:

1. Women cannot engage in competitive job markets where they dominate;
2. Women should stay at home and take care of families and children;
3. Women must avoid any form of participation in politics or business sectors;
4. Men should shoulder all household duties.

Failure to adhere to these policies will have harsh penalties for all who fail to comply. Only those who follow the strict laws can bring prosperity to the country, therefore all other options must be discouraged to ensure compliance.
